[%# wraps-classic
    The compact interface's layout is the classic one, wrapped: the classic
    page is rendered as it would be without this interface, and the compact
    mark and style sheet are added to it. So the navbar, the scripts and the
    body attributes netdisco.js reads are the classic ones, and a change to the
    classic layout, or a site's own layout in template_paths, reaches this
    interface with nothing here to keep in step.

    compact_base_layout is that classic layout's path, given by the web plugin
    UI::Compact (App::Netdisco::Web::Plugin::UI::Compact): it is not looked up
    here as layouts/main.tt, which is this very file from this interface.

    The first line says that a classic override of this layout, a site's, is
    used by this interface: it is not reported as one the interface ignores
    (App::Netdisco::Util::SiteLocal, scan_ui_shadowed). -%]
[% compact_head = BLOCK %]<link rel="stylesheet" href="[% uri_base | none %]/compact/css/compact.css?v=[% asset_version | none %]"/>
</head>[% END %]
[% compact_page = PROCESS $compact_base_layout %]
[% compact_page.replace('<html\b', '<html data-nd-ui="compact"').replace('</head>', compact_head) | none %]
